you were on.
你们来的时候。

1335
00:43:22.520 --> 00:43:23.860
This is Melanie C.
这是梅兰妮·C

1336
00:43:23.920 --> 00:43:28.400
who said, I cannot wait for y'all to get fax machines and fax each
说的，我迫不及待地想看你们买传真机并互相

1337
00:43:28.400 --> 00:43:28.680
other.
发传真了。

1338
00:43:29.140 --> 00:43:31.320
I would also love to have a landline again.
我也很想重新拥有一部座机。

1339
00:43:32.200 --> 00:43:33.220
We never did that.
我们从来没那样做过。

1340
00:43:33.320 --> 00:43:34.560
We never got fax machines.
我们从来没买过传真机。

1341
00:43:34.920 --> 00:43:35.220
I have a landline.
我有一部座机。

1342
00:43:35.680 --> 00:43:36.580
Well, I have a landline.
好吧，我有一部座机。

1343
00:43:36.660 --> 00:43:37.020
We discussed.
我们讨论过。

1344
00:43:37.220 --> 00:43:37.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1345
00:43:37.700 --> 00:43:38.540
I still have it.
我还在用。

1346
00:43:38.540 --> 00:43:42.680
Which is why we were going to get our fax machines and hook them up to our landlines.
这就是为什么我们要买传真机并把它们连到座机上。

1347
00:43:42.920 --> 00:43:43.840
We can still do it.
我们现在还可以这么做。

1348
00:43:44.200 --> 00:43:45.060
I still have a landline.
我仍然有一部座机。

1349
00:43:45.300 --> 00:43:46.340
I'm not getting rid of it.
我是不会把它扔掉的。

1350
00:43:46.480 --> 00:43:46.740
Same.
我也是。

1351
00:43:47.240 --> 00:43:48.920
I'm going down with the landline ship.
我要与座机这艘船共存亡。

1352
00:43:49.600 --> 00:43:49.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1353
00:43:50.520 --> 00:43:51.780
Do they still make faxes?
现在还生产传真机吗？

1354
00:43:52.060 --> 00:43:54.380
Like some, I mean, like doctors still use them, I think, right?
就那种，我的意思是，像医生好像还在用，对吧？

1355
00:43:55.400 --> 00:43:56.100
Doctor's offices?
诊所里？

1356
00:43:56.340 --> 00:43:56.640
Yeah.
对。

1357
00:43:56.700 --> 00:43:57.340
I feel like they're the laSt.
我觉得他们是最后一批了。

1358
00:43:57.360 --> 00:43:57.720
Yes, they do.
对，他们还在用。

1359
00:43:57.800 --> 00:43:58.180
They do.
确实在用。

1360
00:43:58.340 --> 00:43:59.080
So someone makes them.
所以还是有人在制造的。

1361
00:43:59.260 --> 00:43:59.500
There's a staples.
还有史泰博（Staples）。

1362
00:43:59.860 --> 00:44:00.440
You know what?
你知道吗？

1363
00:44:00.440 --> 00:44:01.700
I got to go to Staples after this.
我待会儿得去趟史泰博。

1364
00:44:01.860 --> 00:44:02.280
I'll text you.
我发短信给你。

1365
00:44:02.320 --> 00:44:02.900
Scope it out.
去打探一下。

1366
00:44:03.280 --> 00:44:04.520
See if you see any fax machines.
看看能不能看到什么传真机。

1367
00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:05.520
I'll see what the inventory's like.
我去看看库存情况怎样。

1368
00:44:05.620 --> 00:44:06.960
I want to throw something out there.
我想抛出一个想法。

1369
00:44:06.960 --> 00:44:11.900
This is just part of being a good prepper with our landlines.
这也是我们留着座机的优秀末日求生者的一部分。

1370
00:44:12.140 --> 00:44:13.260
Do you have a wheelbarrow?
你有独轮手推车吗？

1371
00:44:13.700 --> 00:44:14.420
I don't.
我没有。

1372
00:44:14.840 --> 00:44:15.760
You should get one.
你应该买一个。

1373
00:44:16.140 --> 00:44:16.540
Why?
为什么？

1374
00:44:17.340 --> 00:44:18.200
I have a shovel.
我有一把铁锹。

1375
00:44:18.820 --> 00:44:21.600
A shovel is good, but I think you could use a wheelbarrow.
铁锹固然好，但我觉得你用得上独轮手推车。

1376
00:44:21.700 --> 00:44:22.440
I was reading this book.
我最近在读一本书。

1377
00:44:22.560 --> 00:44:27.020
It's called The Wall, and it's about a woman who gets stuck behind an invisible wall, and
书名叫《墙》，讲的是一个女人被困在一堵隐形墙后面，然后

1378
00:44:27.020 --> 00:44:30.440
she only has herself a cow, a dog, and a cat.
她身边只有一头奶牛、一只狗和一只猫。

1379
00:44:30.600 --> 00:44:31.060
It's great.
这本书很棒。

1380
00:44:31.240 --> 00:44:32.580
It's this old novel.
这是一部老小说。

1381
00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:34.040
It's really, really good.
真的非常非常好看。

1382
00:44:34.040 --> 00:44:39.800
And there's only so much farming she can try to do for her own survival and, like, moving
为了自给自足，她能种的庄稼有限，而且比方说还要搬运

1383
00:44:39.800 --> 00:44:41.180
of hay to feed her cow.
干草来喂牛。

1384
00:44:41.700 --> 00:44:44.620
She has to drag it all because she doesn't have a wheelbarrow.
她只能全靠拖拽，因为她没有独轮手推车。

1385
00:44:45.220 --> 00:44:50.440
And it occurred to me, a wagon or a wheelbarrow in end of times would be possibly very helpful.
然后我突然想到，在末日来临时，手推车或独轮车可能会非常有用。

1386
00:44:50.640 --> 00:44:51.500
Just something to think about.
这只是个供参考的想法。

1387
00:44:51.500 --> 00:44:52.280
I'm just going to put it out there.
我只是把它提出来而已。

1388
00:44:52.340 --> 00:44:56.000
I'm just going to piggyback on that and say, do a wagon, not a wheelbarrow.
我顺着这个话题补充一下，选四轮小货车，不要选独轮手推车。

1389
00:44:56.120 --> 00:45:00.420
I don't know when the last time you pushed a wheelbarrow, but I did recently on our farm.
我不知道你上次推独轮手推车是什么时候，但我最近在我们的农场推过。

1390
00:45:00.420 --> 00:45:05.620
And they f***ing suck because if they get, like, heavy on one side or the other, then
那玩意儿真他妈难用，因为如果某一边不小心变重了，

1391
00:45:05.620 --> 00:45:08.040
you're, like, wobbling, and it's just a real pain in the ass.
你就会摇摇晃晃的，简直烦死人了。

1392
00:45:08.060 --> 00:45:08.800
It's a weird design.
这设计挺怪的。

1393
00:45:08.920 --> 00:45:09.600
I hated it.
我讨厌它。

1394
00:45:09.700 --> 00:45:10.720
So maybe wagon then.
那也许选小货车吧。

1395
00:45:11.380 --> 00:45:11.740
Wagon.
小货车。

1396
00:45:12.020 --> 00:45:15.380
Do they make, like, a two-wheeled wheelbarrow, like, with two on the front?
有没有那种双轮的手推车，就是前面有两个轮子的那种？

1397
00:45:15.540 --> 00:45:17.360
Like, why haven't they?
话说，他们为什么不这样做？

1398
00:45:17.540 --> 00:45:18.920
Like, why does it have the one wheel?
为什么非得是一个轮子？

1399
00:45:19.140 --> 00:45:19.900
Why it doesn't?
为什么不呢？

1400
00:45:19.920 --> 00:45:23.020
There's, like, construction worker listeners right now that are just yelling at the phones.
现在肯定有从事建筑行业的听众正对着手机大喊大叫呢。

1401
00:45:23.020 --> 00:45:24.220
That are just yelling at us.
一直在对我们大喊大叫。

1402
00:45:24.220 --> 00:45:29.140
I mean, it is easy with the two arms to dump, you know, the wheelbarrow.
我是说，双把手的车，倒起独轮车来，你知道的，挺轻松的。

1403
00:45:29.360 --> 00:45:29.880
The single wheel.
单轮的。

1404
00:45:30.020 --> 00:45:34.740
The single wheel is easy to dump things, but I found it to push really annoying.
单轮车倒东西很容易，但我发现推起来真的很烦人。

1405
00:45:35.040 --> 00:45:36.680
But you can also pull it behind you.
但你也可以把它拉在身后。

1406
00:45:37.220 --> 00:45:38.320
Yeah, but it's not great.
对，但那感觉不太好。

1407
00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:39.240
Who's doing that?
谁会那样做？

1408
00:45:39.380 --> 00:45:39.840
No one.
没人。

1409
00:45:40.100 --> 00:45:40.700
Probably no one.
可能没人吧。

1410
00:45:40.700 --> 00:45:41.140
No one.
没人。

1411
00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:42.920
You pull a wheelbarrow.
你会拉着独轮车走。

1412
00:45:43.140 --> 00:45:44.660
Oh, wait, there's a two-wheel.
哦，等等，还有双轮的。

1413
00:45:44.860 --> 00:45:46.140
Jordan found a two-wheelbarrow.
乔丹发现了一辆双轮手推车。

1414
00:45:46.260 --> 00:45:46.700
There you go.
这就对了。

1415
00:45:46.740 --> 00:45:46.940
Yes.
是的。

1416
00:45:47.100 --> 00:45:47.280
Yeah.
对。

1417
00:45:47.340 --> 00:45:48.420
That looks like a way better design.
那个设计看起来好多了。

1418
00:45:48.420 --> 00:45:50.880
Okay, so don't use ye olde wheelbarrow.
好吧，所以别用老掉牙的独轮车了。

1419
00:45:51.020 --> 00:45:51.860
Use the new modern one.
用新款现代的吧。

1420
00:45:51.860 --> 00:45:54.300
I don't really have—I don't have a big enough garage for that thing.
我其实没有——我的车库不够大，放不下那玩意儿。

1421
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:56.900
That looks like it takes, like, a big footprint.
那东西看起来挺占地方的。

1422
00:45:57.040 --> 00:45:58.500
That's, like, the size of, like, a motorcycle.
那简直有摩托车那么大。

1423
00:45:59.220 --> 00:46:00.340
You don't have time for that.
你现在可没空搞这个。

1424
00:46:00.980 --> 00:46:01.500
Not yet.
还没呢。

1425
00:46:01.500 --> 00:46:02.460
I got to get a bigger house.
我得换个大房子。

1426
00:46:02.680 --> 00:46:03.180
You get a bigger house.
你得换个大房子。

1427
00:46:03.340 --> 00:46:05.700
My biggest tip—my biggest tip for this is I got to make more money.
我最大的建议——我对此最大的建议是我得赚更多钱。

1428
00:46:05.980 --> 00:46:06.820
You got to make more money.
你得赚更多钱。

1429
00:46:06.820 --> 00:46:08.640
I got to get a bigger house so I can get the wheelbarrow.
我得换个大房子，这样我才能买得起那个独轮车。

1430
00:46:09.100 --> 00:46:12.320
That's—and when you go on a talk show someday and you're like, oh, do you want f***ing money?
那就是——当你哪天去上脱口秀节目，然后别人问你，哦，你想要他妈的钱吗？

1431
00:46:12.320 --> 00:46:14.000
Say, no, I want wheelbarrow money.
你就说，不，我要独轮车钱。

1432
00:46:14.280 --> 00:46:14.480
Yeah.
对。

1433
00:46:14.480 --> 00:46:15.180
That's what I want.
这就是我想要的。

1434
00:46:15.480 --> 00:46:16.280
Filled with cash.
装满现金。

1435
00:46:16.460 --> 00:46:17.260
Yeah, that's it.
对，就是这样。

1436
00:46:17.740 --> 00:46:19.240
Clark, we love you so much.
克拉克，我们太爱你了。

1437
00:46:19.360 --> 00:46:19.940
I love you guys.
我也爱你们。

1438
00:46:19.940 --> 00:46:21.080
Thanks for being here.
谢谢你们来到这里。

1439
00:46:21.380 --> 00:46:21.800
